      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "construe it with शूरः. But no प्रकार is here mentioned. I think",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the reading of C. ought not to have been rejected. It means",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "“ I am complete master of language.” दर्पज्वर see last Stanza and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "note to Nîtis'ataka St. 95 (दर्पामय).—Sragdharâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXXI.—Râmarshi says on this यदा यस्मिन्नवसरे अहं किंचिज्ज्ञः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "अल्पं जानातीति तथा समभवं संजातः तदा........तदा मम मनः. This is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "wrong as introducing तदा twice when it occurs only once in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "the text. किंचित्किंचिदवगतम् = स्तोकं स्तोकं शान्तिवैराग्यप्रतिपादकं शास्त्रम् (Râ-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "marshi.) ज्वरइव = रुद्रकोपोद्भवव्याधिरिव Râmarshi.—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXXII.—लटभ the commentator renders by सलावण्य, I have",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "never seen the word before. समाक्रन्दनगिरः = cries of invocation.—",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXXIII.—खण्डिते = भ्रातृपुत्रादिभिर्विभज्य गृहीते. (Râmarshi) de-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "stroyed or lost seems to be more likely. व्यर्थम् = without obtaining",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "anything. क्षीणे = नष्टधने (Râmarshi) कन्दरदरीकुञ्ज—कन्दर and दरी are",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "given as synonymes in Amara and Medinî. Perhaps therefore the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "reading of N. ought to be preferred as avoiding the pleonasm. Râ-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "marshi renders कन्दर by गव्हरदेशः which would mean a natural cave",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "(Amara.); दरी by गुहा which is the same thing; and कुञ्ज by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "लतादिपिहितोदर as in Amara; and takes the whole to be a Samâhâra-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "Dvandva.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXXIV.—कलितम् might mean बन्धन, but this requires a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "straining. कलिल would seem to be the better reading. चिन्तामणि =",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "the jewel which gives its possessor what he desires. संकल्प =",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "the workings of the mind as in मनः संभोगेभ्यः स्पृहयति न संकल्पविरमम्",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "(Chaṇḍakaus'ika p. 27) or संकल्पप्रभवान्कामांस्त्यक्त्वा सर्वानशेषतः &c.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "(Bhagavadgîtâ VI., 24) on which S'ankara says संकल्पः प्रभवो येषां",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "कामानां ते which shows why संकल्प should be abandoned.—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r8",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXXV.—मौने दैन्यभयम् = In [case of] silence there is the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "danger of being [considered] spiritless. This however destroys",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
